# Findings of the configuration scan that are accepted for this module (S079):
# NONE, and that is a decision left open, not a finding of none. The module is
# implemented as code, checked and never planned or applied, and the first scan of
# it (every severity, the repository's pinned image, offline) reported one HIGH
# finding that is not removed and not accepted here: GCP-0031, "Instance has a
# public IP allocated", on the control plane's one external address, which the
# owner's one address needs to reach the API server. Accepting it, or changing the
# design so that it goes (no external address, the API server behind a load balancer
# or Identity-Aware Proxy), is the owner's decision, in a later change, with the
# reason written above the entry. Its LOW and MEDIUM findings (flow logs, customer-
# managed disk keys) are in the README, for the reader; the scan's recipe lists
# HIGH and CRITICAL only.
#
# An entry would be one Trivy check ID per line, exactly `GCP-` and four digits and
# nothing after it (no expiry, no file name, no wildcard, not the older AVD-
# spelling), and on the line directly above it the reason: what the check says, why
# it holds here, and what a production environment would do instead, in a handful
# of words at least. tests/meridian/test_gcp_kubeadm_scan.py fails on an entry that
# breaks any of this, on an entry at all that its list does not name, on an inline
# ignore comment in a .tf file, on a Trivy configuration or YAML ignore file in this
# directory, and on a second external address or subnet: an entry here applies to
# EVERY resource of the directory, not to one. A finding fixed in the module is
# deleted from here.
